{{!
    Someone else already holds this record.

    Everyone who reaches this page is still a registrant: both claim entry
    points send a member who has finished onboarding to the admin request form
    before any lookup runs. So the page offers no administrator link, which
    would be a member capability this audience cannot reach, and says instead
    when that route becomes available to them.

    Unlike the sibling unavailable page, the two self-serve remedies cannot fix
    this one: the record is held, not unmatched. They are still worth naming,
    because a held record is sometimes a same-name coincidence and a sharper
    match finds the reader's own record instead.
}}

<div class="hero hero-sm">
  <div>
    <h1>{{page.title}}</h1>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="wrapper">
  <section>
    <p>Another member has already claimed this record.</p>

    <p>Sometimes that means two people share a name. If you used a different surname before, or a different email address on the old footbag.org, add either one in the claim step and we will look again for a record of your own.</p>

    <p class="mt-4"><a href="{{content.claimStepHref}}" class="btn btn-primary">Add a Former Name or Old Email</a></p>

    <p class="mt-6">If this really is your record, an IFPA administrator can sort it out once you have finished signing up.</p>

    <p class="mt-6"><a href="{{content.cancelHref}}">Back to the record</a></p>
  </section>
</div>
